{"verdict":"approved","issues":[{"severity":"minor","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":94,"description":"When CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW is \"true\" but CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN is empty (its default), the SDK receives management_token: \"\". Unlike the existing validation for API_KEY, DELIVERY_TOKEN, ENVIRONMENT, and CONTENTSTACK_BRANCH, there is no guard that warns or throws when live preview is enabled without a management token. This could result in silent failures at runtime where the SDK cannot authenticate to fetch draft entries.","suggestedFix":"Add a validation block similar to the existing ones: if (isLivePreviewEnabled && !CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN) { logger.error(\"Contentstack management token not provided for live preview\"); } — or throw if the token is required for the feature to function."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":96,"description":"The fallback endpoint URL \"api.contentstack.io\" is a hardcoded string. Per project convention (criterion 6), endpoint URLs should use named constants. This same value appears in the SDK's own default config, so it is not incorrect, but it would be cleaner to extract it as a named constant (e.g., in src/constants/contentstack.ts) alongside the other Contentstack constants.","suggestedFix":"Export a constant such as DEFAULT_CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_HOST = \"api.contentstack.io\" from src/constants/contentstack.ts and reference it in the service file."}],"summary":"The diff adds Contentstack Live Preview support in two parts: (1) a new enum `ContentstackLivePreviewQueryParams` in src/constants/contentstack.ts exposing the two query-param keys (`live_preview`, `content_type_uid`) the CMS Live Preview pane appends to preview URLs, and (2) conditional SDK configuration in src/services/contentstack.ts that reads three env vars (CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW, CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN, CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_HOST) and, when enabled, adds a `live_preview` config block to the Contentstack Stack options. I confirmed from the installed contentstack SDK (v3.17.2) source that `live_preview` with `enable` and `host` sub-keys is consumed by the SDK's default config and merged via deep-merge — the config is not dead code. The `management_token` is read from an env var (not hardcoded), so no credential leak. The change is concise (~30 lines across 3 files), follows the existing enum pattern in the constants file, and uses conditional spread to avoid mutating the config when live preview is disabled. The spec file was shipped by the pipeline (not the implementer) and tests the enum values correctly. No blockers found. Two minor improvements noted: missing validation for an empty management token when live preview is enabled, and a hardcoded fallback URL that could be a named constant."}
